ulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/2b/2bed1b367cd101e0e90674c619ad87da8c90744df570eeea4d9b0333ccee0de1.png)\n\nNotice that the positive orientations of the outer curve ${C}_{1}$ and the inner curve ${C}_{3}$ are opposite those stated in the question.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-\\left(- \\frac{7}{2}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{14}{3}\\right)-\\frac{20}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-21)+(-28)-40}{6} \\\\  & =- \\frac{47}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544015 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbb58a5e-aca0-59c4-912f-79726bee9634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbb58a5e-aca0-59c4-912f-79726bee9634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544054} :answer-field/id #uuid "dea7cd5a-b58b-58d0-9d87-50e8f2bc76db" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544058}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #u